From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: refuse a mesh vif under NSS offload when mesh is not built

NSS 802.11s mesh offload is not built for this 256 MB board (kuncy7 builds
it for his std group only; an active mesh costs RAM a 256 MB board cannot
spare). With NSS offload on, the firmware then has no mesh vdev, and a
mesh interface configured on an offloaded radio fails deep in
ath11k_nss_vdev_create() (-EINVAL, "unsupported interface type 7"), which
unwinds the half-created vdev and leaves the radio's AP down for good:
`wifi reload` on a radio that carries both an AP and a mesh vif takes the
AP out.

Refuse a mesh vif at the start of add_interface, when NSS offload is on
and NSS mesh is not compiled in, before any vdev or peer is created, so
the AP on the same radio keeps running. 802.11s mesh works in host Wi-Fi
mode (nss.general.wifi_offload=0). The guard compiles out if a future
build enables CPTCFG_ATH11K_NSS_MESH_SUPPORT. Issue #21.

Signed-off-by: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -7231,6 +7231,22 @@
 		goto err;
 	}
 
+	/* NSS 802.11s mesh offload is not built on this board (the 256 MB
+	 * boards leave it out; see ath.mk). With NSS offload on, the firmware
+	 * has no mesh vdev, so bringing a mesh interface up fails late and
+	 * takes the radio's AP down with it. Refuse it here, before anything
+	 * is created, so the AP on the same radio stays up; mesh runs in host
+	 * Wi-Fi mode (nss.general.wifi_offload=0). If a future build enables
+	 * CPTCFG_ATH11K_NSS_MESH_SUPPORT this guard compiles out.
+	 */
+#ifndef CPTCFG_ATH11K_NSS_MESH_SUPPORT
+	if (ab->nss.enabled && vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT) {
+		ath11k_warn(ab, "NSS offload: 802.11s mesh is not supported on this build; set nss.general.wifi_offload=0 for mesh\n");
+		ret = -EOPNOTSUPP;
+		goto err;
+	}
+#endif
+
 	/* an AP_VLAN ext vdev left over from before a restart */
 	if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN)
 		ath11k_core_nss_stale_ext_vdev_release(ar, arvif);
